# Peer resolution is strict (default): typescript-eslint 8.70.0 declares peer
# eslint "^8.57.0 || ^9.0.0 || ^10.0.0", so the pinned ESLint 10.14.0 now
# satisfies it and no legacy-peer-deps flag is needed. (Previously, with
# typescript-eslint 8.46.0, .npmrc needed legacy-peer-deps=true because its
# peer range stopped at ESLint 9; see ADR-001.)
